# UI stack and quality gates

## ShadCN + Tailwind

- Reuse primitives from `@/components/ui/*`; add new ones via the ShadCN CLI / `components.json`, not one-off copies.
- Style with Tailwind utilities and existing theme tokens in `src/index.css` (CSS variables). Avoid new CSS frameworks or inline style systems.
- Compose with `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` when merging classes.

## ESLint + typecheck + tests

- Match `frontend/eslint.config.js` (TypeScript + react-hooks). Do not disable rules to hide issues.
- Keep code type-safe: no unjustified `any`; prefer explicit Query/Mutation generics.
- **Unit (Vitest):** co-located `*.test.ts(x)` under `src/`; keep `npm test` green.
- **UI integration (Playwright):** FE-only browser flows in `frontend/e2e/ui-integration/`.
- **E2E (Playwright):** API/service-backed journeys in `frontend/e2e/system/`.
- UI integration and E2E are a different strategy from unit tests — never under `src/`, never via Vitest. Prefer `npm run test:ui-integration` / `npm run test:e2e:system`, or `npm run test:e2e` for both. To watch the browser: `npm run test:ui-integration:headed` or `npm run test:e2e:ui`. Not on Husky pre-commit.
- Pre-commit runs lint, typecheck, and unit tests when `frontend/` changes — fix failures instead of bypassing hooks.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — custom button + untyped fetch bypassing UI kit and typecheck
<button style={{ color: 'blue' }} onClick={() => fetch('/x')}>Save</button>

// ✅ GOOD — ShadCN + Tailwind tokens + typed handlers
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button'

<Button type="button" variant="secondary" onClick={onSave}>
  Save
</Button>
```

From `frontend/`: `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm test`; Playwright via `npm run test:ui-integration`, `npm run test:e2e:system`, or `npm run test:e2e`.
